                  <td>Conduction (Ultra-Pocketable)</td>
                  <td>Best Discreet Stealth Design</td>
                  <td>$320 – $380 AUD</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><strong>XMAX V3 Pro</strong></td>
                  <td>Convection on a Budget</td>
                  <td>Best Value Under $150</td>
                  <td>$120 – $150 AUD</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>

            <h3>1. Storz & Bickel Mighty+ — The Undisputed King</h3>
            <p>Manufactured in Germany, the Mighty+ features ceramic-coated heating chambers, USB-C rapid charging (80% in 40 minutes), and a 60-second heat-up time. Its hybrid heating system ensures dense, cool, effortless clouds from the very first draw. For Australian medical cannabis patients, the Mighty Medic edition is listed on the ARTG, reinforcing its safety and build quality.</p>

            <h3>2. TinyMight 2 — The Convection Powerhouse</h3>
            <p>Crafted in Finland using American walnut wood, stainless steel, and quartz glass, the TinyMight 2 delivers massive instant vapor clouds in just 3 to 5 seconds. It offers dual operating modes: on-demand (instant draws when pressing the button) and session mode (continuous heat).</p>

            <h3>3. Arizer Solo 3 — Phenomenal Flavor & Battery Stamina</h3>
            <p>Canadian manufacturer Arizer equipped the Solo 3 with an upgraded hybrid heating oven and an isolated all-glass vapor path that keeps your cannabis tasting unadulterated. Its massive dual internal lithium battery delivers up to 3 hours of continuous session runtime.</p>
          </section>

          <section id="convection-vs-conduction">
            <h2>Convection vs Conduction: Understanding the Difference</h2>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Conduction Heating:</strong> Heat is transferred directly through physical contact with the oven walls (like a fry pan). Conduction vapes (e.g., Pax Plus) are compact and fast, but can cook the herb between draws.</li>
              <li><strong>Convection Heating:</strong> Hot air is drawn through the ground flower only when you inhale (like a convection oven). Convection vapes (e.g., TinyMight 2) preserve exceptional terpene flavor and waste zero herb while idling.</li>
              <li><strong>Hybrid Heating:</strong> Combines conductive oven walls with incoming hot air (e.g., Mighty+, Arizer Solo 3). This delivers the dense cloud volume of conduction paired with the efficiency and flavor of convection.</li>
            </ul>
          </section>

          <section id="temp-guide">
            <h2>Optimal Cannabis Vaping Temperature Chart (°C)</h2>
            <p>Fine-tuning your vaporizer temperature gives you complete control over which cannabinoids and terpenes are vaporized:</p>

            <table class="price-table">
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th>Temperature Range</th>
                  <th>Key Compounds Activated</th>
                  <th>Sensory & Therapeutic Effects</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td><strong>160°C – 175°C (Low)</strong></td>
                  <td>Beta-Caryophyllene, Pinene, Myrcene</td>
                  <td>Maximum flavor profile, very light vapor, uplifting mental clarity, anti-inflammatory relief without heavy sedation.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><strong>175°C – 190°C (Medium)</strong></td>
                  <td>THC (Boils at 157°C), Limonene, Terpinolene</td>
                  <td>The sweet spot for daytime medication. Balanced physical and mental relaxation with moderate cloud density.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><strong>190°C – 205°C (High)</strong></td>
                  <td>Linalool, Humulene, CBD (180°C)</td>
                  <td>Full-bodied clouds, deep muscle relaxation, mood calming, significant physical tension relief.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><strong>205°C – 220°C (Max)</strong></td>
                  <td>CBN, THCV, CBC</td>
                  <td>Heavy nighttime sedation, couch-lock sensation, maximum extraction for chronic discomfort or insomnia.</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </section>

          <section id="dry-herb-vs-carts">
            <h2>Dry Herb Vapes vs 510 THC Vape Cartridges</h2>
            <p>Many Australian consumers ask whether they should invest in a dry herb vaporizer or purchase pre-filled 510 THC cartridges. Both methods offer distinct advantages:</p>

            <div class="info-box">
              <h4>Choose a Dry Herb Vaporizer If:</h4>
              <p>You love the ritual and aroma of whole natural flower, want access to hundreds of diverse cannabis cultivars, or wish to save your Already Vaped Bud (AVB) to make potent homemade cannabutter.</p>
              <p><a href="/shop/flower/" style="color:var(--color-eucalyptus); font-weight:700; text-decoration:underline;">Explore Clean Australian Cannabis Flower &rarr;</a></p>
            </div>

            <div class="info-box" style="background:#f0fdfa; border-color:#99f6e4;">
              <h4>Choose 510 THC Vape Carts & Pens If:</h4>
              <p>You need maximum stealth with zero smell, instant one-second vapor on the go, zero grinding or oven packing, and ultra-high potency (75%–90% THC).</p>
              <p><a href="/shop/vapes/" style="color:var(--color-eucalyptus); font-weight:700; text-decoration:underline;">Browse 510 THC Cartridges & Rechargeable Vape Pens &rarr;</a></p>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="tga-reforms">
            <h2>Australian Vape Laws & TGA Medical Approvals (2024–2026)</h2>
            <p>Australia's vaping framework distinguishes between commercial nicotine vapes and medical dry herb inhalation devices. Under current Therapeutic Goods Administration (TGA) regulations, dry herb vaporizers intended for use with prescribed therapeutic cannabis are recognized as legitimate medical devices.</p>
            <p>Ensure that whichever device you use is crafted from food-grade or medical-grade materials (such as PEEK plastics, borosilicate glass, or titanium) to ensure zero off-gassing at high temperatures.</p>
          </section>

          <section id="faqs">
            <h2>Frequently Asked Questions About Vaporizers in Australia</h2>
            <div class="faq-list">
              {vapeFaqs.map((faq) => (
                <div class="faq-item" style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem; padding: 1.25rem; background: var(--color-surface, #f8fafc); border-radius: 8px; border-left: 4px solid var(--color-primary, #2D5A4A);">
                  <h3 style="margin-top: 0; font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--color-text, #1e293b);">{faq.q}</h3>
                  <p style="margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--color-text-muted, #475569);">{faq.a}</p>
                </div>
              ))}
            </div>
          </section>

          <section class="conclusion">
            <h2>Summary</h2>
            <p>Switching from combustion to vaporization is one of the most beneficial upgrades you can make for your respiratory health and your wallet. By vaporizing at controlled temperatures, you preserve expensive cannabinoids, savor true terpene profiles, and eliminate harmful toxins. Explore our hardware catalog and clean flower selections to find the ideal match for your routine.</p>
